<article class="env-lemma" id="0FVR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FVR">Lemma <span data-tag="0FVR">45.14.10</span>.</a> Assume given data (D0), (D1), and (D2') satisfying axioms (A1) – (A7). If $k'/k$ is a Galois extension, then we have $\int _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')} 1 = [k' : k]$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We observe that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k') \times \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k') = \coprod \nolimits _{\sigma \in \text{Gal}(k'/k)} (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\sigma ) \times \text{id})^{-1} \Delta  \]
</div>
    <p>
       as cycles on $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k') \times \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')$. Our construction of $\gamma $ always sends $[X]$ to $1$ in $H^0(X)$. Thus $1 \otimes 1 = 1 = \sum (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\sigma ) \times \text{id})^*\gamma ([\Delta ])$. Denote $\lambda : H^0(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')) \to F$ the map from axiom (A6), in other words $(\text{id} \otimes \lambda )(\gamma (\Delta )) = 1$ in $H^0(\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k'))$. We obtain 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \begin{align*}  \lambda (1) 1 &  = (\text{id} \otimes \lambda )(1 \otimes 1) \\ &  = (\text{id} \otimes \lambda )( \sum (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\sigma ) \times \text{id})^*\gamma ([\Delta ])) \\ &  = \sum (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\sigma ) \times \text{id})^*( (\text{id} \otimes \lambda )(\gamma ([\Delta ])) \\ &  = \sum (\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(\sigma ) \times \text{id})^*(1) \\ &  = [k' : k] \end{align*}
</div>
    <p>
       Since $\lambda $ is another name for $\int _{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')}$ (Remark <a href="/tag/0FIK" data-tag="0FIK">45.14.6</a>) the proof is complete. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>